From 3a95c041e5c2011b51472fb22005b72055864278 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Linus Walleij <linusw@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:58:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: broadcom: Assemble the BCM6846 Runner program at build
 time

Move the reduced BCM6846 Runner program from the register initialization
array to a symbolic source file. Add a two-pass flex/bison assembler,
organized around a scanner, grammar, symbol table and instruction encoder
as in aicasm. Resolve labels and constants, check operand bounds and keep
fixed entry-point assertions for the host context ABI.

Generate big-endian instruction bytes and embed them in a read-only
binary object linked into the Ethernet driver. Load the image with the
Runner helper at the original instruction-RAM initialization step.
Preserve the complete vendor image, including NOP padding, and the order
of all other initialization writes.

Document the encoding evidence from the reduced, CFE2 and PON images.
Use symbolic names for decoded forms while retaining explicit fields
for unresolved control and peripheral operations. Packet-notification
semantics are not established by this conversion; RX still uses the
existing polling fallback.

Add host tests for the original-image digest, encoding vectors, labels,
expressions, field limits and malformed input.

Signed-off-by: Linus Walleij <linusw@kernel.org>

---
